In that single-realization comparison, OU--III has the lowest mean normalized
vertical-displacement RMS error: 6.6\% of $H_s$, compared with 8.2\% for
OU--II, 12.3\% for the adaptive PII observer, and 15.0\% for the adapted
TVG--NLO. These values establish a reproducible four-method reference but are
not ensemble estimates and are not used to claim statistical superiority.

